{"content":[{"c":["HERMON, Mount"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Mountain often mentioned as the northern extremity of the territory conquered by Joshua and Moses in Transjordan; it is also the northern boundary of the inheritance of the half-tribe of Manasseh as well as of Israel in general (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.8","r":"Deut.3.8","rawR":"Deut.3.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.8","value":"Deut.3.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:8"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.4.48","r":"Deut.4.48","rawR":"Deut.4.48","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.4.48","value":"Deut.4.48"}],"t":"ref","v":"4:48"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.17","r":"Josh.11.17","rawR":"Josh.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.17","value":"Josh.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.12.1,5","r":"Josh.12.1,5","rawR":"Josh.12.1,5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.12.1,5","value":"Josh.12.1,5"}],"t":"ref","v":"12:1, 5"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.11","r":"Josh.13.11","rawR":"Josh.13.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.11","value":"Josh.13.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:11"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Chr.5.23","r":"1Chr.5.23","rawR":"1Chr.5.23","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Chr.5.23","value":"1Chr.5.23"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Chr 5:23"},"). Hermon is said to tower over the valley of Lebanon (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.17","r":"Josh.11.17","rawR":"Josh.11.17","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.17","value":"Josh.11.17"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:17"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Josh.13.5","r":"Josh.13.5","rawR":"Josh.13.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.13.5","value":"Josh.13.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"13:5"},") and over the land of Mizpah in the valley of Mizpah, to which Joshua pursued the kings of Canaan after his victory over them at the waters of Merom (",{"href":"?bref=Josh.11.3,8","r":"Josh.11.3,8","rawR":"Josh.11.3,8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Josh.11.3,8","value":"Josh.11.3,8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jos 11:3, 8"},"). Biblical poetry praises Hermon for its height and for causing dew on Zion (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.133.3","r":"Ps.133.3","rawR":"Ps.133.3","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.133.3","value":"Ps.133.3"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 133:3"},"), and it was famed for its wildlife (",{"href":"?bref=Song.4.8","r":"Song.4.8","rawR":"Song.4.8","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Song.4.8","value":"Song.4.8"}],"t":"ref","v":"Sg 4:8"},"). It also appears in tandem with Mt Tabor (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.89.12","r":"Ps.89.12","rawR":"Ps.89.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.89.12","value":"Ps.89.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 89:12"},") and with the Jordan (",{"href":"?bref=Ps.42.6","r":"Ps.42.6","rawR":"Ps.42.6","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ps.42.6","value":"Ps.42.6"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ps 42:6"},"). The mountain itself is about 13 miles (21 kilometers) long and rises to a height of 9,166 feet (2.8 kilometers)."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"HermonMount","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Dt 3:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.8","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.8","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.8"},{"anchorText":"4:48","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.4.48","rawQueryValue":"Deut.4.48","sourceRefExact":"Deut.4.48"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.17","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.17","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.17"},{"anchorText":"12:1, 5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.12.1,5","rawQueryValue":"Josh.12.1,5","sourceRefExact":"Josh.12.1,5"},{"anchorText":"13:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.11","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.11","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.11"},{"anchorText":"1 Chr 5:23","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Chr.5.23","rawQueryValue":"1Chr.5.23","sourceRefExact":"1Chr.5.23"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:17","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.17","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.17","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.17"},{"anchorText":"13:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.13.5","rawQueryValue":"Josh.13.5","sourceRefExact":"Josh.13.5"},{"anchorText":"Jos 11:3, 8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Josh.11.3,8","rawQueryValue":"Josh.11.3,8","sourceRefExact":"Josh.11.3,8"},{"anchorText":"Ps 133:3","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.133.3","rawQueryValue":"Ps.133.3","sourceRefExact":"Ps.133.3"},{"anchorText":"Sg 4:8","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Song.4.8","rawQueryValue":"Song.4.8","sourceRefExact":"Song.4.8"},{"anchorText":"Ps 89:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.89.12","rawQueryValue":"Ps.89.12","sourceRefExact":"Ps.89.12"},{"anchorText":"Ps 42:6","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ps.42.6","rawQueryValue":"Ps.42.6","sourceRefExact":"Ps.42.6"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"a8e128834408b0c78abcd287972f20946cdd16a862da530239c7f80dc4080bdd","sourceItemName":"HermonMount","sourceItemOrder":265,"sourceMember":"Articles/H.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[{"name":"AerialViewOfMountHermon","src":"../Pictures/Pictures.xml"}]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"HermonMount","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Hermon, Mount","title":"Hermon, Mount","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}